      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T03:56:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These two are (or will be) in v6.13-rc1. The idea is to cherry-pick these and the in-flight I2C OF component prober (https://lore.kernel.org/all/20241106093335.1582205-1-wenst@chromium.org/) to the android-6.12-desktop kernel. AFAIK I\u0027m supposed to pick these to android-mainline and they will trickle over automatically?",
      "parentUuid": "9575b38f_73c3a294",
      "revId": "0db4eef5ac03e3f0719bd3a42c75b44feb6b5e51",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ef4317f_0e501128",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-28T16:29:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "v6.13-rc1 will be merged into android-mainline in a not too distant future -- I\u0027ll let Lee and/or Greg comment on that, but that should be a matter of days/weeks after Linus has released rc1 hopefully. So these two patches will land with the rest of the rc1 patches.\n\nUnless there is a tight project deadline and this cannot wait a few days (which would surprise me for anything based on android-mainline) I\u0027m not sure if there is that much value in actively cherry-picking them, all that should happen naturally 😊",
      "parentUuid": "7d642df1_407a1b85",
      "revId": "0db4eef5ac03e3f0719bd3a42c75b44feb6b5e51",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eaf48fff_422c0558",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3733995
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-29T04:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seems fine then. Would I still need to cherry-pick them into android-6.12 / android-desktop-6.12, or does that happen automatically? (Assuming this happens before the GKI stable KMI cutoff date.) The Android kernel stuff is all still new to me.",
      "parentUuid": "2ef4317f_0e501128",
      "revId": "0db4eef5ac03e3f0719bd3a42c75b44feb6b5e51",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "494a2a6e_c190de52",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-29T10:09:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will merge the upstream -stable 6.12.x branch regularly into android16-6.12, so if your patch gets picked up as a -stable fix you shouldn\u0027t need to do anything if it can wait for that to happen. Otherwise, you can absolutely cherry-pick it yourself into android16-6.12. (Cherry-picking UPSTREAM patches into \u0027release\u0027 branches is very common and perfectly accepted, it\u0027s really just cherry-picking into android-mainline that I found unusual since it is supposed to track upstream by construction).\n\nI hope that helps, thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "eaf48fff_422c0558",
      "revId": "0db4eef5ac03e3f0719bd3a42c75b44feb6b5e51",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
